# Semgrep ignore patterns (gitignore syntax).
#
# The deprecated, non-production Python layer is excluded from the SAST gate.
# Production runtime is Rust-only (weissman-server, weissman-worker,
# fingerprint_engine); legacy/python-src is scheduled for removal (see
# legacy/README.md). Its only SAST findings are false positives — e.g.
# vault_client.py logs the *key identifier* (`key`, `role`), never the secret
# value, which the logger-credential-leak heuristic can't distinguish. Gating
# active development on dead-code false positives is not useful; the Rust
# production code is still fully scanned.
#
# Root-level src/ and tests/ are symlinks into legacy/, so exclude those too.
legacy/
/src/
/tests/
